   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Find the value of \\( \\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} + h\\right)^{3} - \\frac{1}{8}}{h} \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         3,
         4
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The numerator has the form \\( f(\\frac{1}{2} + h) - f(\\frac{1}{2}) \\) with \\( f(x) = x^{3} \\), because \\( f(\\frac{1}{2}) = \\frac{1}{8} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            8
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "So the function is \\( f(x) = x^{3} \\) and the base point is \\( x = \\frac{1}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The limit is the definition of \\( f'(\\frac{1}{2}) \\), and \\( f'(x) = 3 x^{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            3,
            [
               "Power",
               "x",
               2
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Evaluate: \\( f'(\\frac{1}{2}) = \\frac{3}{4} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            3,
            4
         ]
      }
   ],
